# 실시간 추적 서버(8090)의 실행 파일. 명령줄 옵션과 동작은 한 파일이던 때와 같다.
# 실제 코드는 옆의 src/ 폴더에 일(검출 detect, 추적 track, 재식별 reid, 카메라 camera, 짐벌 gimbal, 웹 화면 web, 공통 common)별로 들어 있고,
# 여기서는 본체(src/app.py 의 main)를 불러 실행만 한다. 바로 아래 영어 설명은 나누기 전 파일 맨 앞에 있던 기록 그대로다.
"""LWIR tracker on the DX-M1 (model bank package, final version 2026-11-03) = feattrk/m1_track_eval_v11.py with the research-harness assumptions removed
(no git-branch assertion, no default data folder, native_post.py/post.so next to this file, join_tiles copied in). Algorithm and outputs unchanged.
Run from this folder after `bash setup.sh`; see the model bank README section "추적 시스템" for the full command.
The rest of this docstring is the research script's own history; options not listed in the README are research options.

M1 ONLINE pipeline (main session runs it on the M1; this task only wrote and dry-ran it on the PC):
  2026-11-01 e2e30 copy (claude_tracking_reacq_20261031/m1_newm/e2e30, generated by make_e2e_script.py from claude_vit_reid_01): adds
  --det rt480 = new m RT480 PTQ tiles NEWMRT480A (frame rows 16:496, cols 0:384) on NPU_0 + NEWMRT480B (rows 16:496, cols 256:640) on
  NPU_1, join_tiles + fast_nms, y + 16 to frame coords (pre/post = m1_flir_eval_pipe.py NEWMRT480); every other path is unchanged.
  v2 (make_e2e_script_v2.py): --gmc = BoT-SORT camera-motion compensation (Ultralytics GMC sparseOptFlow + STrack.multi_gmc), default off.
  v3 (make_e2e_script_v3.py): --class-gate = person tracks only with person detections, car/truck only among themselves (claude_review_fixes_01
  classgate port; allowed with bytetrack and rebind, not with the ViT), default off.
  v4 (feattrk, 11-02): --data <frame folder with coco.json> (default = the FLIR video test).
  v5 (feattrk, 11-02, user 'M1에서해'): --relabel <re-ID DXNN> = lost-track ID relabel (relabel_online.OnlineRelabel, PREREG_RELABEL_M1.json)
  on top of the UNCHANGED tracker (--tracker bytetrack --no-vit [--class-gate]): synchronous batch-1 crops on NPU_2 right after the tracker
  update (every frame <= --rl-new-k crops of new IDs awaiting a decision + every --rl-every frames <= --rl-k refresh crops); only person IDs
  change. TRACKS.jsonl = relabelled rows, TRACKS_BASE.jsonl = the tracker rows, RELABEL_LOG.json, RESULT.json 'relabel'. Default off.
  v6 (feattrk, 11-02, user 'fps 제한 없애고 성능 제일 좋은 걸 뽑아봐'): --gmc-ds / --gmc-corners / --gmc-mindist = GMC downscale, max corners and
  minimum corner distance (defaults 2 / 1000 / 1 = unchanged Ultralytics sparseOptFlow); gmc_speed_replay.py chose 300 corners, distance 5.
  v7 (feattrk, 11-02, user '현재 m 파일로 속도만 높이는 걸 고민해보자' -> '응 진행해봐'): speed options that leave every output unchanged:
    --gmc-thread   optical flow (GMC) of frame k computed in one worker thread as soon as frame k is read (overlaps the NPU detection);
                   the worker runs frames in order with a fresh GMC per video, so the warps equal the serial ones (needs --pipeline)
    --npu-depth D  D frames read + submitted ahead (D output buffers per detector tile engine, buffer_count D); D = 1 = the v6 pipeline
    --rl-async     KeepID refresh crops submitted asynchronously on NPU_2 (own engine, N slots) and collected at the next frame
                   (relabel_online embed_async; identical result with --rl-new-k >= pending IDs, e.g. 99)
    --ort-threads  intra-op threads of the CPU part of the DXNNs (detector: 8 output memory ops; default 1 = unchanged)
  v8 (feattrk, 11-02): --preload decodes every frame into memory before the loop (a camera delivers frames in memory), so the frame
  period is the plain wall-clock interval with no JPEG decode inside it: v7 subtracted the decode time from the interval, which overstates the
  rate once another thread (the --gmc-thread worker) is the bottleneck. Outputs unchanged.
  v9 (feattrk, 11-02, user decision 'zoom'): --zoom = zoom re-detection of SMALL AMBIGUOUS person outputs (default off = every output byte-identical
  to v8). Candidates = the normal tiles' DECODED pre-NMS anchors of frame i-1 (jo480: person is the top class, --zoom-lo <= score < --zoom-hi, box
  height < --zoom-maxh), light NMS .5 among them, top --zoom-max by score (+ lost person tracks' predicted boxes with --zoom-lost). Each candidate
  gets a square context window (side = max(--zoom-ctx x h, --zoom-min), shifted into the frame) cut from the CURRENT frame i, upscaled INTER_LINEAR
  so the person becomes ~--zoom-target px tall (cap --zoom-maxscale), shelf-packed into ONE 480x384 canvas (pad = mean gray of frame i) that the
  SAME NEWMRT480A DXNN, loaded a second time on NPU_2 (Engine key 'ZOOM', depth 1), re-detects. Timing: the canvas is built + submitted at the end
  of iteration i-1 (after the tracker / KeepID of i-1; frame i's gray is already in 'ahead'), collected at iteration i right after detect(i): same
  dec480-style Decoder + fast_nms, boxes mapped back through the window that holds their centre, accepted if person, conf >= --zoom-acc, mapped
  height < --zoom-acch, IoU <= .5 against every normal detection (conf >= .10, classes 0/2/6) of frame i, NMS .5 among the accepted; the survivors
  are appended to frame i's detection array BEFORE the tracker (also to PRED_NEWMRT480.jsonl with a 'zoom' 0/1 flag list). Ambiguous candidates
  are never output by themselves. RESULT.json 'zoom' (candidates / windows / accepted per frame, canvas_ms, wait_ms, merge_ms, NPU ms), ZOOM_LOG.json.
  zoom_wait_ms + zoom_merge_ms are excluded from tracker_ms; canvas_ms is inside frame_total / latency / period. Requires --det rt480 --pipeline --no-vit.
  v11 (feattrk, 11-03): --confirm-gate <GATE_GRU32_FROZEN.json> = the LEARNED confirmation gate (failure_analysis_20261102/track_gate, GRU32, thr_out 0.3, thr_low 0,
  no tent_low) replaces 3FrameConfirm inside the bytetrack tracker (GateTracker; needs --tracker bytetrack --class-gate --no-vit; works with or without
  --judge). Boxes of the tracker rows change (that is the gate's job); with --gate off the output is byte-identical to v10. Output tag '_cgate'. RESULT.json 'gate'. (--gate stays the v4 association distance gate.)
  v10 (feattrk, 11-02): --judge <RELINK_JUDGE_FROZEN.json> = the LEARNED relink judge (failure_analysis_20261102/learned_relink, frozen logistic model
  lr_B_real_K0, threshold 0.40, decision at the birth frame) replaces KeepID's hand rule inside the --relabel path: relink_online_judge.OnlineJudge
  (numpy only) takes OnlineRelabel's place with the same online bookkeeping (same step() call, same rl engine on NPU_2, --rl-async honoured for the
  refresh crops), computes the ~80 causal pair features of every (new ID, lost candidate <= 90 frames) pair exactly as learned_relink/build/
  relink_data.py defines them, scores them with the frozen model and relabels one-to-one, forward only (new ID takes the candidate's output ID;
  boxes / FP / FN unchanged). Crop policy on NPU_2 changes from KeepID's 'clean crops only' to 'every output person crop >= 32 px' under a per-frame
  budget --judge-crops N (default 2): the new IDs' own crops first (births with candidates, then other births), then refresh of the tracks with the
  fewest / oldest features; missing features are the availability flags of the training tables (NaN -> training median + missing flag).
  --rl-every / --rl-k / --rl-new-k are ignored with --judge. Output folder tag '_judge' (+ '_jc<N>' when N != 2). RESULT.json 'judge' (births,
  evaluated, relabels, ms per decision = features + model, crops embedded, NPU_2 time). Default off = every output byte-identical to v9.
  NPU_0/NPU_1 : YOLO26m-RT DRT512A/B tiles exactly as m1_vit_eval.py / m1_flir_eval.py (same timing scope for det_total_ms)
  NPU_2       : ViT re-ID student, BATCH 1 (--vit <name>.dxnn, input uint8 NHWC [1,H,W,3], output [1,128]), at most ONE job
                in flight; every --vit-every N frames up to --k crops are queued (priority: (a) person detections that started a
                new track this frame = re-bind candidates, (b) tracks that just became lost and have no gallery feature (crop
                from the previous frame at their last box), (c) round-robin refresh of active tracks). Jobs are submitted /
                collected at two sync points per frame (right after the detector submit and right after the detector wait),
                so each crop overlaps either the detection or the host post-processing. Embeddings are keyed to the (frame,
                detection) they came from and attached to the track that owned that detection, 1-2 frames late.
  CPU         : tracker in the same loop (self-contained numpy + scipy.optimize.linear_sum_assignment; no lap/ultralytics):
                --tracker bytetrack = IoU-only two-stage ByteTrack-like, buffer 30 (baseline A)
                --tracker rebind    = + lost-track re-bind within 2 x height, guard IoU .3, buffer 60 (B when --no-vit)
                                      + with the ViT: a late appearance re-bind: when the embedding of a NEW track arrives and a
                                      LOST track within the radius has cosine >= --sim with it, the new track takes the lost id (C)
Outputs (<out>/): TRACKS.jsonl (project format: image_id, coco_image_id, video_id, tracker_reset, tracks_xyxy_id_conf_class_detectionindex,
frame coords 512x640), PRED_DRT512.jsonl, RAW_TIMINGS.json, RESULT.json (det_total/tracker/vit/frame_total ms p50/p95/p99, crops/s delivered,
NPU ms, core utilisation, rebinds). Guard: waits while another m1_*eval*.py runs (copied from m1_two_tower75_eval.py). --prepare builds
upload_track/ on the PC. --mock runs the same loop on the PC with a fake dx_engine (TorchScript B0 trace + folded student) for a dry run.
--vit-bench-n N (default 0 = off; requires --no-vit): ViT COST bench - N synchronous batch-1 crops per frame on NPU_2 after NMS, embeddings
discarded, so the frame period / latency show how many crops per frame fit (RESULT.json 'vit_bench').
--vit-budget N --vit-priority lostfirst (default 0 = off): LostFirstTracker - at most N synchronous batch-1 ViT crops per frame for all
priorities together (P1 gated re-identification candidates > P2 at-risk > P3 just-lost > P4 round-robin), no asynchronous queue
(RESULT.json 'vit_budget'); with --sim 0.6 --gate 3.5 --vit-budget 2 = the offline choice G1_A1_g3.5_s0.6_N2 (tracker_ab/VITBUDGET_KO.md).
--n-init N (default 2 = unchanged) / --radius R (default 2.0 = unchanged), added 2026-10-23 from idsw_fix/ix_tracker.py FixTracker (F4 n_init,
F5 radius): N = matched frames, the birth frame included, before a NEW track is output (2 = birth frame + 1 hit = the current rule, 1 behaves
the same; tracks born on a video's first frame are still output at once); R = motion re-bind radius in lost-track heights. The offline
choice --n-init 3 --radius 1.5 (idsw_fix/RESULT_KO.md, C_F4_n3+F5_r1.5) was verified only with --tracker rebind --no-vit."""
from src.app import main


if __name__ == '__main__':
    main()
